========================================================================
A. ODD-CYCLE PAYMENT LEMMA — how many struts can an odd cycle carry
========================================================================
  A cycle with n_s struts and n_c cables needs (mod 2pi)
      sum_cables +-phi  ==  pi * n_s .
  Reachability over the sign choices: the set of reachable residues of a
  sum of n_c terms, each in +-B(omega). Scan omega.
  triangle (length 3):
    n_s=0: PAYABLE for omega in [1.394, 2.700]  (x in [0.062, 0.900])
    n_s=1: NOT payable at any omega in window
    n_s=2: NOT payable at any omega in window
    n_s=3: NOT payable at any omega in window
  pentagon (length 5):
    n_s=0: PAYABLE for omega in [1.394, 2.700]  (x in [0.062, 0.900])
    n_s=1: PAYABLE for omega in [1.939, 2.700]  (x in [0.062, 0.413])
    n_s=2: PAYABLE for omega in [1.939, 2.700]  (x in [0.062, 0.413])
    n_s=3: NOT payable at any omega in window
    n_s=4: NOT payable at any omega in window
    n_s=5: NOT payable at any omega in window
  heptagon (length 7):
    n_s=0: PAYABLE for omega in [1.394, 2.700]  (x in [0.062, 0.900])
    n_s=1: PAYABLE for omega in [1.939, 2.700]  (x in [0.062, 0.413])
    n_s=2: PAYABLE for omega in [1.939, 2.700]  (x in [0.062, 0.413])
    n_s=3: PAYABLE for omega in [1.939, 2.700]  (x in [0.062, 0.413])
    n_s=4: PAYABLE for omega in [1.939, 2.700]  (x in [0.062, 0.413])
    n_s=5: NOT payable at any omega in window
    n_s=6: NOT payable at any omega in window
    n_s=7: NOT payable at any omega in window

  => TRIANGLES admit NO struts (all-cable wound m=1 only, omega <= ~2.09).
     PENTAGONS admit at most 2 struts. Parity alone (bipartization) badly
     UNDERSTATES the demotion cost: geometry windows bite harder than Z2.
========================================================================
B. FRUSTRATION INDEX (graph-only lower bound) vs THE REAL COST
========================================================================
  K4 (tetrahedral frame)   n= 4 E= 6  maxcut= 4  frustration index (edges to delete for bipartite) = 2
  triangular prism         n= 6 E= 9  maxcut= 7  frustration index (edges to delete for bipartite) = 2
  cube                     n= 8 E=12  maxcut=12  frustration index (edges to delete for bipartite) = 0
  pentagonal prism         n=10 E=15  maxcut=13  frustration index (edges to delete for bipartite) = 2
  hexagonal prism          n=12 E=18  maxcut=18  frustration index (edges to delete for bipartite) = 0
  icosahedron (5-reg)      n=12 E=30  maxcut=20  frustration index (edges to delete for bipartite) = 10
  dodecahedron             n=20 E=30  maxcut=24  frustration index (edges to delete for bipartite) = 6
  The ledger/brief expectation 'a 3-regular closed strut shell is
  over-constrained by exactly 2 => demote 2 links' matches the frustration
  index only for K4 and the triangular prism — and even there DEMOTION !=
  DELETION: a demoted link still carries its cycle phase, and part A shows
  triangles cannot be paid by 1 or 2 cables. The real minimum demotions:
    K4:               no consonant realization AT ALL (part C)
    triangular prism: 6 cables (both triangles all-cable), 3 vertical struts (part D)
    cube:             0 (bipartite, all-strut) — the H-series selection rule
    pentagonal prism: 10 cables (both pentagons), 5 vertical struts (part D)
    hexagonal prism:  0 — BIPARTITE (all faces even). Ledger P4's 'over-
                      constrained by 2' is REFUTED: it needs no demotion.

========================================================================
C. K4 IS DEAD — the diagonal-hole argument + exhaustive check
========================================================================
  All triangles => all-cable (part A). All-cable K4 = 4 phases pairwise
  in the allowed band S = B u (2pi-B). Pigeonhole: 4 points on the circle,
  the two 'diagonal' pairs have separation = sum of two adjacent gaps in
  [2*lo, 2pi-2*lo]; the band's hole (omega*dmax, 2pi-omega*dmax) swallows
  that whole interval whenever omega*dmax < 2*omega*dmin + hole-margin.
  Numeric check over the full window:
  omega=1.394 band=[1.394,2.111] hole=(2.111,4.172): best residual^2 = 0.4522  => infeasible
  omega=1.600 band=[1.600,2.503] hole=(2.503,3.780): best residual^2 = 0.243  => infeasible
  omega=1.900 band=[1.900,3.068] hole=(3.068,3.215): best residual^2 = 0.4394  => infeasible
  omega=2.094 band=[2.094,3.431] hole=(3.431,2.852): best residual^2 = 1.096  => infeasible
  omega=2.400 band=[2.400,4.002] hole=(4.002,2.282): best residual^2 = 2.022  => infeasible
  omega=2.700 band=[2.700,4.559] hole=(4.559,1.724): best residual^2 = 0.09418  => infeasible
  (diagonal separations forced into [2*lo, 2pi-2*lo] which sits inside the hole)

